# UIS Enabled Services
# Format: One SCRIPT_ID per line
# Run 'uis list' to see available services
# Run 'uis enable <service>' to add a service
# Run 'uis disable <service>' to remove a service

# === Core (default) ===
nginx

# === Monitoring ===
# prometheus
# grafana
# loki
# alloy        # ships container logs into Loki - without it Loki stays empty
# uptime-kuma        # external watchdog - run it OUTSIDE the cluster it monitors

# === AI ===
# openwebui
# ollama

# === Databases ===
# postgresql
# redis

# === Storage ===
# minio

# === Integration ===
# rabbitmq
# temporal

# === Analytics ===
# Dagster orchestrates DATA ASSETS (lineage, freshness, dbt). Temporal above
# orchestrates DURABLE PROCESSES. They are not alternatives - see the docs.
# dagster

# === Automation ===
# browserless is what makes Uptime Kuma's `real-browser` monitor type usable —
# without it that monitor type has no browser to connect to.
# browserless

# === Applications ===
# nextcloud

# neko — the shared human+agent browser. DELIBERATELY COMMENTED OUT, and in no
# stack, so it can only ever start from an explicit `./uis deploy neko`.
# It keeps its logins between sessions and exposes UNAUTHENTICATED full browser
# control over CDP to anything in the cluster. Read
# /docs/services/automation/neko before enabling it.
# neko
